GNU Zebra
*********

   `GNU Zebra' is a Routing Software which provides TCP/IP based
routing protocols such as RIP, OSPF, BGP and so on.  Zebra turns your
machine into a full powered router.  Zebra is multi-server routing
software.  Each daemon has it's own terminal interface which called VTY,
so you can dynamically change configuration and view routing information
while daemon is running.

   This is beta-edition version 0.2 of `GNU Zebra Manual' for alpha-01
version of `GNU Zebra'.

   This manual describes `zebra' and some other beasts.

