Overview of `Zebra'
*******************

   Today TCP/IP network is covering all over the world.  The Internet
has deployed many countries and companies.  If you are connecting to the
Internet or using TCP/IP LAN network, you will need IP Routing.

   `GNU Zebra' is a free software which provides Distributed Routing
System.  It includes many protocol specific daemons.  `RIPd' handles
RIP protocol. `OSPFd' is off course a daemon which supports OSPF
version 2 described in RFC2178.  `BGPd' daemon supports BGP-4 protocol
described in RFC1771 (A Border Gateway Protocal 4).  `zebra' is routing
manager and it dose kernel routing table management.

